Use cFTModalPanel.pkg         // FT: the dark modal, same base as MaintainLibrariesFT.dg
Use cTimer.pkg                   // oCwPollTimer - the poll that makes this genuinely asynchronous
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use FTPageIsUp.pkg               // FT: FTHostPageIsUp - can the host's page take a live push now?
Use cFTGridHost.pkg              // FT: the dialog's one host - a grid of 8 px columns, the page over its Close button (RDCFlexTron)
Use FTAllWebControlClasses.pkg   // FT: cFTWebButton - Close
Use cFTHtmlPage.pkg              // FT: the run's page - its title (psLabel) and the glyph beside it
Use cLibraryInventory.pkg        // SwsFormatOf - the verdict comes from the FILE
Use cWorkspaceCopyPlan.pkg       // UnresolvableLibraryRefs - the chain walk that names what df-cli tripped on
Use cRDCAsyncProcess.pkg            // the process itself; started, then polled
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg         // the HTML vocabulary - OpenHtml, IconLabel, the builders
Use RefactorFileIO.pkg           // rfOpenOutput / rfCloseOutput - channel file I/O
Use cEncodingHelpers.pkg         // rfHtmlEscape and the encoding helpers
Use cDfCliPackages.pkg           // DfCliPath / DfCliCapture - the df-cli that does the conversion

/*  CONVERTING A WORKSPACE .sws FROM INI TO DATAFLEX 26 JSON - with the wait on screen.

    WHY A DIALOG AND NOT A STATUS PANEL (Nils 2026-08-14). df-cli's convert can take a while, and
    every earlier attempt at showing that went wrong in the same way: the work blocked the message
    pump, so whatever was on screen froze, and a frozen thing is indistinguishable from a hung one.
    This is the version that does not block.

    GENUINELY ASYNCHRONOUS, which the earlier ones were not. RDCRunProgramBounded STARTS the child
    asynchronously and then sits in a polling loop - so the process is async and the application is
    not. Here the poll lives on a cTimer instead, which is exactly the use cRDCAsyncProcess's own header
    describes. Between ticks the UI is live: the CSS bar animates by itself, the output area fills,
    and the panel repaints because nothing is holding the pump.

    THE OUTPUT IS THE POINT. df-cli explains itself perfectly well - "Failed to load workspace. Would
    you like to attempt a repair? (y/n):", or the list of projects it could not find - and the
    program has been paraphrasing that at second hand. Captured through the cmd.exe redirect
    DfCliCapture already uses, then tailed on every tick, it is simply shown.

    AND THE PROMPT CANNOT HANG US. StartProcess passes CREATE_NO_WINDOW, so the child has no console:
    a read from stdin FAILS instead of waiting for a human. The question still lands in the log,
    where it becomes the explanation rather than a deadlock. That is the whole lesson of 2026-08-14
    turned into a feature.

    A MARQUEE, NOT A MEASUREMENT. df-cli reports no progress, so the bar is a pure CSS animation that
    says "still working" and claims no percentage. It moves on its own; no DataFlex tick drives it.

    THE VERDICT COMES FROM THE FILE, never the exit code: the only question is whether the .sws is
    JSON now, and the file is the one witness that cannot be wrong.

    A PAGE OVER ITS CLOSE BUTTON (2026-09-30), built the way the library's message box is: one grid
    host, which cFTModalPanel fits to the panel (phoClientHost); the run in a cFTHtmlPage, whose title
    names the target version; and Close as a framework button (cFTWebButton) under it, shut until there
    is a verdict. Until then Close was a chip in the page's HTML footer. df-cli's output keeps its own
    scroll box inside the page, so the verdict under it stays in view however long the output grows.  */

Object oConvertWorkspace_dg is a cFTModalPanel
    Set Label to "Convert workspace to the DataFlex 26 format"
    Set Size to 230 620
    Set Location to 2 6
    Set piMinSize to 170 500
    Set Icon to "DFRefactor.ico"

    // The .sws to convert. Never assumed to be the loaded workspace - the migration flow points this
    // at a copy that is not open yet.
    Property String  psSwsFile ""
    // The version written into the converted file. The caller floors this at 26.0; nothing here does.
    Property String  psTargetVersion "26.0"
    // Where cmd.exe is told to put df-cli's stdout+stderr, and what the tail re-reads each tick.
    Property String  psLogFile ""
    // Everything read from that log so far, already escaped for HTML.
    Property String  psOutput ""
    // The async child, and how long it has been going.
    Property Handle  phProc 0
    Property Integer piElapsedMs 0
    // False while it runs; True once there is a verdict. Drives the bar, the Close button and OnTimer.
    Property Boolean pbFinished False
    // The answer the caller gets: is the file JSON now?
    Property Boolean pbConverted False
    // Why it failed, when it did. Shown under the output rather than in a second dialog - a modal on
    // top of a modal is how the confirm dialog's web host got broken in the first place.
    Property String  psVerdict ""
    // The programs the INI file listed before df-cli ran, for the check that every one arrived.
    Property String[] pasListedProjects
    // True when the converted file lacks one of them: the verdict names it, in the failure style.
    Property Boolean pbProgramsLost False

    Object oWebHost is a cFTGridHost
        Set Location to 4 4
        Set Size to 206 612
        Set peAnchors to anNone         // placed by cFTModalPanel (phoClientHost)
        // Row 0, the page, takes the extra height, and row 1 is 8 px of air above Close in row 2. Column 0 takes
        // the extra width, so Close keeps to the right edge; the page spans every column.
        Set piColumnCount to 12         // column 0, then Close's 11
        Set psColumnWidths to "0/1fr"   // column 0 takes the extra width
        Set psRowHeights to "0/1fr 1/8px"

        // A path, and df-cli's own words, are DATA here - not markup. "R&D" is an ordinary folder
        // name and an unescaped & silently truncates what follows it.
        Function Esc String sText Returns String
            Function_Return (rfHtmlEscape(sText))
        End_Function

        // The page's body: the file, the bar while df-cli works, its output and the verdict. The heading is the
        // page's own title (ShowTitle), and Close is a framework button under the page.
        Function BodyHtml Returns String
            String sHtml sSws sOut sVerdict
            Boolean bDone bOk bLost

            Get psSwsFile       of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to sSws
            Get psOutput        of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to sOut
            Get pbFinished      of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to bDone
            Get pbConverted     of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to bOk
            Get psVerdict       of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to sVerdict
            Get pbProgramsLost  of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to bLost

            // The stylesheet, every rule in it scoped to the body's .cw; the palette's tokens come with the host.
            Move (CssLink("convertworkspace")) to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("cw")) + (DivOpen("cw-p")) + (Esc(Self, sSws)) + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
            If (bDone = False) ;
                Move (sHtml + (((DivOpen("cw-bar")) + '<i></i>') + CS_DivEnd)) to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("cw-out"))) to sHtml
            If (Trim(sOut) = "") ;
                Move (sHtml + ((SpanOpen("cw-wait")) + 'df-cli is running. Its output appears here as it arrives') + CS_Ellipsis + CS_SpanEnd) to sHtml
            Else ;
                Move (sHtml + sOut) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml

            If (bDone = True) Begin
                // A conversion that lost a program is not shown as a success (2026-09-11).
                If (bOk = True and bLost = False) ;
                    Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("cw-v cw-ok")) + (Esc(Self, sVerdict)) + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
                Else ;
                    Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("cw-v cw-bad")) + (Esc(Self, sVerdict)) + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
            End

            Move (sHtml + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
            Function_Return sHtml
        End_Function

        /* Row 0: the run. The title names the target version, so ShowTitle sets it on each open; the literal is the
           Designer's. */
        Object oCwPage is a cFTHtmlPage
            Set piRowIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 12
            Set pbFillHeight to True        // the body fills the page; df-cli's output scrolls in its own box
            Set psLabel to "Converting to the DataFlex 26.0 JSON workspace format"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftpage ftg-export"
            /* A SAMPLE FOR THE STUDIO'S DESIGNER, which draws a literal psHtml: BodyHtml's markup for a run that has
               just started, with a made-up path. The program never shows it - Activating renders the real run
               before the page loads (RefreshBody). */
            Set psHtml to """
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="CssStyle/convertworkspace.css">
            <div class="cw">
                <div class="cw-p">C:\Projects\Order Entry\Order Entry.sws</div>
                <div class="cw-bar"><i></i></div>
                <div class="cw-out"><span class="cw-wait">df-cli is running. Its output appears here as it arrives&hellip;</span></div></div>
            """
        End_Object

        /* Row 2: CLOSE, a framework button (cFTWebButton, RDCFlexTron) at the bottom right. It is shut until df-cli
           has finished and there is a verdict (RefreshBody); its OnButtonClick runs after the web click has returned
           (the library's click relay), where the panel can close. 11 columns (78 px) fit the caption (Close ~72 px,
           measured 2026-09-30). */
        Object oCwCloseBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piRowIndex to 2
            Set piColumnIndex to 1
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Close"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-close"
            Set pbEnabled to False
            Set psToolTip to "Wait for df-cli to finish."

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send CloseNow of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    // cFTModalPanel fits the host to the panel, when it is shown and on every resize.
    Set phoClientHost to (oWebHost(Self))

    /* THE PAGE AND CLOSE from the dialog's state - on each open and on every tick of the poll. UpdateHtml keeps
       the page for a mount still to come and pushes it to a page that is up; the button's setter WebSets the same
       way. Close opens when there is a verdict - pushed when that changes, not on every tick. */
    Procedure RefreshBody
        Handle hoHost hoPage hoClose
        String sHtml
        Boolean bDone
        Move (oWebHost(Self)) to hoHost
        Move (oCwPage(hoHost)) to hoPage
        Move (oCwCloseBtn(hoHost)) to hoClose
        Get BodyHtml of hoHost to sHtml
        Send UpdateHtml of hoPage sHtml
        Get pbFinished to bDone
        Send UpdateEnabled of hoClose bDone
        Send UpdateToolTip of hoClose (If(bDone, "", "Wait for df-cli to finish."))
        Send CheckUpdateWebUI of hoHost
    End_Procedure

    /* THE TAIL. Re-reads the whole log each tick rather than tracking an offset: it is a handful of
       lines, and a length-based tail would be trusting a size Windows can report STALE while the
       writer still holds the handle (see the note in feedback about open-handle file sizes).

       A read that fails is not an error - cmd.exe may hold the file at the moment we look - so the
       previous text simply stands until the next tick.

       EACH LINE AS ITS BYTES ARE (Nils 2026-09-30: a workspace named "... with åäö" showed here as
       "... with Õõ÷"). df-cli writes its own messages in the Windows code page, and this read them as
       OEM - the BOM rule's answer for a file without one. rfReadToolOutputLines reads a line as UTF-8
       when its bytes are UTF-8, in the Windows code page otherwise - as cDfCliPackages reads df-cli. */
    Procedure PullOutput
        String[] asLines
        String sLog sOut
        Integer i iMax

        Get psLogFile to sLog
        If (sLog = "" or vFilePathExists(sLog) = 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move (rfReadToolOutputLines(sLog)) to asLines
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iMax
        If (iMax < 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move "" to sOut
        For i from 0 to iMax
            Move (sOut + (Esc(oWebHost(Self), asLines[i])) + Character(10)) to sOut
        Loop
        Set psOutput to sOut
    End_Procedure

    /* THE POLL. 250ms - fast enough that output feels live, slow enough that re-reading a short log
       costs nothing. Everything that decides the outcome happens here; Popup just waits for Close. */
    Object oCwPollTimer is a cTimer
        Set piTimeout to 250
        Set pbEnabled to False

        Procedure OnTimer
            Handle  hoProc hoPlan
            Boolean bRunning bDone
            Integer iElapsed iFormat i
            String  sSws sVerdict sTarget
            String[] asListed asNow asLost asBad
            Handle  hoInv

            Get pbFinished of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to bDone
            If (bDone = True) Begin
                Set pbEnabled to False
                Procedure_Return
            End

            Get phProc of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to hoProc
            If (hoProc = 0) Begin
                Set pbEnabled to False
                Procedure_Return
            End

            Send PullOutput of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self))
            Get IsProcessRunning of hoProc to bRunning
            Get piElapsedMs of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to iElapsed
            Move (iElapsed + 250) to iElapsed
            Set piElapsedMs of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to iElapsed

            // Still going, and inside the deadline: repaint and come back.
            If (bRunning = True and iElapsed < (CI_DfCliConvertTimeoutSecs * 1000)) Begin
                Send RefreshBody of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self))
                Procedure_Return
            End

            Move "" to sVerdict
            If (bRunning = True) Begin
                Send KillProcess of hoProc 1
                Move ("df-cli did not finish within" * String(CI_DfCliConvertTimeoutSecs) * "seconds and was stopped.") to sVerdict
            End
            Send CleanUp of hoProc
            Send Destroy of hoProc
            Set phProc of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to 0
            Set pbEnabled to False

            // One last read - the final lines usually land as the process exits.
            Send PullOutput of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self))

            /* ASKED OF THE FILE. Whatever df-cli said and whatever it returned, the question is
               whether the .sws is JSON now. */
            Get psSwsFile of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to sSws
            Get Create (RefClass(cLibraryInventory)) to hoInv
            Get SwsFormatOf of hoInv sSws to iFormat
            Send Destroy of hoInv
            Set pbConverted of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to (iFormat = eSwsJson)

            If (iFormat = eSwsJson) Begin
                Move "Converted. The workspace file is now in the DataFlex 26 JSON format, and packages can be added to it." to sVerdict
                /* EVERY PROGRAM MUST ARRIVE (Nils 2026-09-11). What the INI file listed is checked
                   against what the JSON file lists now, read the way the Compile program list
                   reads it. The section was renumbered before df-cli ran, so this should find
                   nothing - it is here so that a program df-cli drops for any other reason is
                   named, not found missing later. */
                Get pasListedProjects of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to asListed
                Get GetWorkspaceProjects of ghoApplication sSws to asNow
                Move (SwsProgramsMissing(asListed, asNow)) to asLost
                If (SizeOfArray(asLost) > 0) Begin
                    Move (sVerdict * SwsProgramsMissingNote(asLost)) to sVerdict
                    Set pbProgramsLost of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to True
                End
            End
            Else If (sVerdict = "") Begin
                Move "NOT converted - the file is still in the older INI format. df-cli's own output is above; a library reference that does not resolve is the usual cause, because df-cli reads the whole chain before it converts anything." to sVerdict
                /* NAME THE ENTRY (2026-09-14). On a real workspace df-cli's account above was a dump
                   of a library file's own text and "Failed to load/install library X"; the chain walk
                   knows which entry that is, and whether the file is missing or is there carrying
                   git conflict markers. The same walk the copy step reports with. */
                Get psTargetVersion of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to sTarget
                Get Create (RefClass(cWorkspaceCopyPlan)) to hoPlan
                Get UnresolvableLibraryRefs of hoPlan sSws sTarget to asBad
                Send Destroy of hoPlan
                If (SizeOfArray(asBad) > 0) Begin
                    Move (sVerdict + " These references do not resolve:") to sVerdict
                    For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(asBad) - 1)
                        Move (sVerdict + " [" + asBad[i] + "]") to sVerdict
                    Loop
                End
            End
            Set psVerdict   of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to sVerdict
            Set pbFinished  of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to True
            Send RefreshBody of (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self))
        End_Procedure
    End_Object

    // Close, from its button's OnButtonClick - after the web click, where the modal can end. The button is shut
    // until there is a verdict, so this needs no guard of its own.
    Procedure CloseNow
        Send Close_Panel
    End_Procedure

    // The page's title names the version the file is converted to - stored for a page that loads, and pushed to a
    // page that is up.
    Procedure ShowTitle String sTarget
        Handle hoHost hoPage
        String sTitle
        Move (oWebHost(Self)) to hoHost
        Move (oCwPage(hoHost)) to hoPage
        Move ("Converting to the DataFlex " + sTarget + " JSON workspace format") to sTitle
        Set psLabel of hoPage to sTitle
        // A push only for a page that is up (RDCFlexTron's FTHostPageIsUp: the host active, its page called
        // home). This runs as the dialog opens, when its page is still to be built - and on a second opening
        // the framework's own flag alone still said "ready", for the page of the first.
        If (FTHostPageIsUp(hoHost)) ;
            WebSet psLabel of hoPage to sTitle
    End_Procedure

    /* Start the child, then hand over to the timer. Called from Activating rather than before Popup
       because the web host has to be alive for the first paint to reach it. */
    Procedure Activating
        String sDfCli sSws sTarget sLog sHome sArgs
        String[] asNone
        Handle hoProc
        Boolean bOk
        Integer iPos

        Forward Send Activating

        Set psOutput    to ""
        Set psVerdict   to ""
        Set pbFinished  to False
        Set pbConverted to False
        Set piElapsedMs to 0
        Set pasListedProjects to asNone
        Set pbProgramsLost to False

        Get psSwsFile to sSws
        Get psTargetVersion to sTarget
        Send ShowTitle sTarget
        Get DfCliPath to sDfCli
        If (sDfCli = "" or sSws = "") Begin
            Set psVerdict  to "df-cli.exe was not found beside the selected compiler, so nothing could be converted."
            Set pbFinished to True
            Send RefreshBody
            Procedure_Return
        End

        // The workspace's own folder: where the log goes, and where the child runs.
        Move (RightPos("\", sSws)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sSws, iPos)) to sHome
        Else ;
            Move ".\" to sHome
        Move (sHome + "dfrefactor_convert.log") to sLog
        If (vFilePathExists(sLog)) ;
            Move (rfDeleteFile(sLog)) to bOk
        Set psLogFile to sLog

        /* THE PROGRAM LIST GOES IN WHOLE (Nils 2026-09-11). df-cli's convert keeps only the LAST of
           two [Projects] lines that share a key, and says nothing about the one it drops - a real
           workspace lost its main program that way. So the section is renumbered Project0..N
           first, every program kept; a healthy file is not touched, and a JSON one has no
           [Projects] to touch. What the file listed is kept as well, so the verdict can check that
           every program arrived. */
        Set pasListedProjects to (SwsIniProjectsFromLines(rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sSws)))
        If (SwsIniRenumberProjectsInFile(sSws) = False) Begin
            Set psVerdict  to "NOT converted. The [Projects] list in this file had to be renumbered first - df-cli drops a program when two share a number - and the file could not be written. It may be read-only, or open in the Studio."
            Set pbFinished to True
            Send RefreshBody
            Procedure_Return
        End

        /* THE cmd.exe WRAPPER, exactly as DfCliCapture builds it - cmd strips the first and last
           quote of the /c argument, so the real command is wrapped in a second pair. It is what
           makes stdout+stderr capturable at all.

           Started through cRDCAsyncProcess so the poll can live on the timer, and with bShowWindow
           False so CREATE_NO_WINDOW applies: no console means df-cli's repair prompt fails fast
           instead of waiting for an answer nobody can give. The question still reaches the log. */
        Move ('/c " "' + sDfCli + '" convert --df ' + sTarget + ' "' + sSws + '" > "' + sLog + '" 2>&1 "') to sArgs
        Get Create (RefClass(cRDCAsyncProcess)) to hoProc
        Get StartProcess of hoProc "cmd.exe" sArgs sHome False to bOk
        If (bOk = False) Begin
            Send CleanUp of hoProc
            Send Destroy of hoProc
            Set psVerdict  to "df-cli could not be started."
            Set pbFinished to True
            Send RefreshBody
            Procedure_Return
        End
        Set phProc to hoProc
        Send RefreshBody
        Set pbEnabled of (oCwPollTimer(Self)) to True
    End_Procedure
End_Object

/*  Convert sSwsFile to the DataFlex 26 JSON workspace format, showing the run.

    Returns True when the file is JSON afterwards - which is asked of the FILE, not of df-cli's exit
    code. sTargetVersion is written into the converted workspace; the CALLER floors it at 26.0,
    because a target below that has no packages to record and no reason to convert.

        Get ConvertWorkspaceToJson sSws sTarget to bOk

    Global, so both the Libraries dialog and the migration copy can reach it.  */
Function ConvertWorkspaceToJson Global String sSwsFile String sTargetVersion Returns Boolean
    Handle ho
    Boolean bOk

    Move (Trim(sSwsFile)) to sSwsFile
    If (sSwsFile = "") ;
        Function_Return False
    If (Trim(sTargetVersion) = "") ;
        Move "26.0" to sTargetVersion

    Move (oConvertWorkspace_dg(Self)) to ho
    Set psSwsFile       of ho to sSwsFile
    Set psTargetVersion of ho to sTargetVersion
    Send Popup of ho
    Get pbConverted of ho to bOk
    Function_Return bOk
End_Function
